Z||000000||GTMike||11-07-2001||02:28 AM||||well i participated in my first illegal street drag races.   i only raced two times and i was so ashamed.   i only got beet by about 5 feet but still.  i felt bad.  <P>it was a 90's 2 door  5-speed barreta.  with a 3.1 and a custum exaust and a 160 t-stat and chip.  <P>it was my first ever street race.  i was was nervous.  the flag guy said ok i'm going to count to 3 them put my arms down.   so he put up one then two then three fingers then put he arms down.  we were off  he had a better reaction time.  thats where he got the jump about 5 feet.  and thats the way it stayed till the finish. <P>i'll never race again with this engine.  hope to get a 3.4 in over thanksgiving.  <P>then only good thing is  everyone liked my fiero the loved the sound. and i beat a suberu 2.5 rs 5-speed.<P> on our way up the foot hills, threw the turns my car left everyone.  there was a WRX in the lead then me then a riced out civic. and a long line of other cars.  there were alot of turns and me and the wrx would put  250 yards on the other cars in the turns.    both the wrx guy and the riced civic guy were like wow. your car handles good.   <P> i may go and watch the races but  i wont be racing untill i can get a 3.4 in.    <P>i still can't believe i got beat by a bareta<P>------------------<BR>87GT mostly stock, cold air intake, no cat. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtmike1_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||LoW_KeY||11-07-2001||02:42 AM||||Whoa.. odd.. I've raced many with my 2.8 and spanked them.. the 3.4 you won't notice much of a difference.. <P>It's a tad bit peppier but a 3.4 won't massively stomp a 2.8, but when I had my old 2.8 it was a great running motor strong as hell! <P>every race I have I do get nervous some times and mess up on the start but I usually catch'em, but if I do get the start I want its crazy cause the car launches like crazy!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||11-07-2001||03:20 AM||||i hear that fieros with the 3.4 run like 14.7s.    thats a full second faster then the 2.8.   its also a better building block for what i want to do.   some stronger pistons and a 50 shot of nos to start then when the money comes in.   a trubo kit with aound 7 lbs of boost.  <P>i use to have a girlfriend that had the same kind of car, barreta v6  but with and auto and my car was alot faster. maybe he was just a good driver.  oh well just more motivation for me to save my money. <p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||11-07-2001||08:27 AM||||Don't feel bad, Berettas are pretty quick.  My friend has a 3.1 with only minor bolt-ons, and he's done 15.2 on the 1/4 mile.  The Quad 4 powered Beretta is even quicker!  I'm 99% sure I couldn't beat my friends Beretta; he's got an auto that helps accelerate a lot quicker on drags, and some real sticky, wide tires (compared to ours).  They're a pretty close race.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||11-07-2001||08:39 AM||||Don't give up racing! Just because you lost once dosen't mean you will again. Even if you do its mostly for fun anyway. You will allways do better then next time.<BR>I'll race just about anybody in any car I happen to be driving. I have a blast even if I do lose, if I win its even more fun though   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Don't feel too bad, I lost to a 4 door lumina in my 88 coupe.... Im guessing he probably had a 3.1 also.<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
